# Implementation Plan - SIMAD oLearn UI Prototype

This plan outlines the creation of a high-fidelity HTML/CSS prototype for the SIMAD oLearn Student Dashboard.

## Goal Description
Create a visually stunning, responsive, and accessible UI sample for the Student Dashboard. This will verify the design aesthetic and core usability concepts outlined in the specs.

## User Review Required
> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Aesthetics**: The design must feel "premium" and "modern", avoiding generic Bootstrap/Tailwind looks.
> **Branding**: Must prominently display "SIMAD oLearn".

## Proposed Changes

I will create a new directory `ui_prototype/` containing:

#### [NEW] ui_prototype/index.html
*   **Header**: Logo, User Profile, Notifications.
*   **Sidebar**: Navigation (Dashboard, Courses, Exams, Calendar, Support).
*   **Main Content**:
    *   **Welcome Widget**: "Good Morning, Amina".
    *   **Active Exam Card**: High-priority "Exam Shield" launch area.
    *   **Course Grid**: Visual cards for enrolled courses with progress bars.
    *   **Upcoming Deadlines**: Timeline view.

#### [NEW] ui_prototype/styles.css
*   **Variables**: HSL color palette (SIMAD Brand Colors: likely Blue/Gold/White based on typical university themes, but I will choose a modern "Academic Blue" and "Growth Green" palette).
*   **Layout**: CSS Grid and Flexbox.
*   **Typography**: Inter or Roboto (Google Fonts).

## Verification Plan
### Manual Verification
*   **Visual Check**: Open `ui_prototype/index.html` in the browser.
*   **Responsive Check**: Resize window to mobile width to verify layout adaptation.
